## 5. Load the source files

Run `01_ingestion/01_download_adventureworks_source.py`.

It downloads 17 AdventureWorks files from the Microsoft `sql-server-samples`
GitHub repository into
`/Volumes/smart_factory_dev/raw/landing_files/batch/erp/<area>/<entity>/`.

The files are tab separated with no header row. That is why the Auto Loader
options use `sep: "\t"` and `header: "false"`.

Then run `01_ingestion/02_verify_landing_files.py` and confirm you see 17 files.

---

## 6. Run the pipeline

### Option A, the job (recommended)

Open **Jobs & Pipelines**, find `[dev] Smart Factory Medallion Pipeline` and
click **Run now**. It runs seven tasks in order and takes about 9 minutes on a
small cluster.

To make it run by itself when new data lands, add a file arrival trigger on
`/Volumes/smart_factory_dev/raw/landing_files/batch/erp`.

### Option B, notebook by notebook

Useful when you are debugging one layer.

```
02_bronze/19_run_all_bronze.py
03_silver/19_run_all_silver.py
04_gold/13_run_all_gold.py
06_pytest/00_run_pytest.py
```

Each `run_all` notebook calls the individual notebooks with `%run`, in dependency
order.

Before running `00_run_pytest.py`, open it and change `test_folder` to your own
workspace path. It is currently hardcoded to one user.

---

## 7. Check the run

```sql
-- audit history
SELECT * FROM smart_factory_dev.monitoring.<audit_table> ORDER BY 1 DESC LIMIT 20;

-- row counts
SELECT 'bronze' AS layer, count(*) FROM smart_factory_dev.bronze.customer
UNION ALL
SELECT 'silver', count(*) FROM smart_factory_dev.silver.customer;

-- anything quarantined
SHOW TABLES IN smart_factory_dev.silver LIKE '*quarantine*';

-- SCD Type 2 sanity check, should return zero rows
SELECT ProductID, count(*) AS current_rows
FROM smart_factory_dev.gold.dim_product
WHERE IsCurrent = true
GROUP BY ProductID
HAVING count(*) > 1;
```

There are also validate notebooks per layer: `02_bronze/18_validate_bronze.py`,
`03_silver/18_validate_silver.py`, `04_gold/12_validate_gold.py`.

