## 10. Common problems

**`PERMISSION_DENIED` on the external location.** The access connector does not
have Storage Blob Data Contributor on the storage account, or the storage
credential name in the notebook does not match the one in Unity Catalog.

**Auto Loader reads nothing.** The checkpoint already recorded the files. To
reload from scratch, delete the checkpoint folder for that entity:

```python
dbutils.fs.rm("/Volumes/smart_factory_dev/raw/checkpoint_files/bronze/product", True)
```

**Bronze row counts look wrong.** The files have no header row. If `header` is
set to `true` anywhere, the first data row is eaten as column names.

**pytest cannot find the tests.** `test_folder` in `06_pytest/00_run_pytest.py`
is an absolute workspace path tied to one user. Change it to yours.

**`audit_failure` runs but the job shows success.** It should not. If it does,
check that the failure notebook still raises at the end instead of only printing.

**Bundle deploy fails on the cluster id.** The default in `databricks.yml` points
at a cluster that no longer exists. Pass your own with `--var`.

---

## 11. Cleaning up

Cost comes almost entirely from the cluster. Set auto termination to 10 to 20
minutes.

To remove everything:

```bash
databricks bundle destroy -t dev
```

```sql
DROP CATALOG IF EXISTS smart_factory_dev CASCADE;
```

Then delete the storage container in Azure. Dropping the catalog does not delete
files in external locations.